      <P><FONT face=3DVerdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif color=3D#ffffff =
size=3D2>
      <DIV>
      <DL>
        <DT>12/23/03 to 12/25/03=20
        <DD>Did some reverse engineering of the Caglec 452 Baud Rate =
Generator=20
        (M452 replacement) for Robert K. Managed to figure out what the =
jumpers=20
        and switches do.
        <P></P>
        <DT>12/20/03 to 12/23/03=20
        <DD>Worked with Tim on the RS-232 interface for his 8i.
        <P></P>
        <DT>12/11/03=20
        <DD>Fiddled some more with the idea of NVRAM based PDP-8i =
memory.=20
        Managed to clear up most of the mystery about how the memory bus =
works=20
        (but not the pin-out).
        <P></P>
        <DT>12/10/03=20
        <DD>Experimented with the idea of making replacement memory for =
the=20
        PDP-8i based on NVRAM. Got a little mired down trying to =
understand how=20
        the 8i memory works. Also exposed a discrepancy between the =
memory bus=20
        description in the 8i schematics and in the MC8i schematic.
        <P></P>
        <DT>12/07/03=20
        <DD>"Finished" working on the paddle connector design with Guy =
S., at=20
        least until someone wants to order boards. Thanks, Guy!
        <P></P>
        <DT>12/06/03=20
        <DD>Continued to work issues in the paddle connector design with =
Guy S.
        <P></P>
        <DT>12/05/03=20
        <DD>Started working on design of paddle connectors for =
Posibus/Negibus=20
        connectors.
        <P></P>
        <DT>12/04/03=20
        <DD>Put together a parts order for a reader-run mod. Maybe I =
should make=20
        that a project, as there seem to be a number of people which =
have TTYs=20
        that need one.
        <P></P>
        <DT>12/03/03=20
        <DD>Got the W076x board artwork accepted. Parts came from =
JameCo, so I=20
        built 12 parts kits. Ran out of .1uf capacitors, so I'll have to =
order=20
        some more.
        <P></P>
        <DT>12/02/03=20
        <DD>Ordered the W076x boards.
        <P></P>
        <DT>12/01/03=20
        <DD>Ordered the M452X boards and the parts from JameCo. Had to =
rework=20
        the silkscreen for the board shop. Got the oscillators from =
DigiKey.
        <P></P>
        <DD>Also got the current loop connectors from DataTerm.
        <P></P>
        <DD>Got the resistance info on the reader-run relay and modified =
the=20
        reader-run circuit to match, though it is clear there is =
weirdness in=20
        the reader-run mod relative to the drawings.
        <P></P></DD></DL><!--"''"--></DIV></FONT>
      <P></P><!--/area Type=3D"main"--></TD>
